{
  "id": "functional-data-analysis",
  "term": "functional data analysis",
  "definition": "Functional data analysis is a way of studying data that change over time by treating them as continuous trajectories rather than isolated measurements. It can be used to examine individual patterns, average change across a group, and the main kinds of variation over time, often summarizing complex trajectories with a small number of principal components.",
